{"id":"commit:71d9f4aafad91566417932f11bb28fac40798597","ts":"2026-06-09T04:03:45-07:00","kind":"commit","commit":"71d9f4aafad91566417932f11bb28fac40798597","title":"feat(shell): click-to-zoom mermaid lightbox (theme-aware)","why":"Click any rendered mermaid diagram to open a pan/zoom lightbox: wheel-zoom\nanchored at cursor, drag-pan, +/-/reset/close controls, ESC/overlay to close.\n\nThe enlarged image re-renders the diagram source under the active shell\ntheme via a per-diagram %%{init: theme}%% directive (light->default,\ndark->dark), so it matches the page theme and stays consistent with the\nin-content render -- instead of cloning the already-themed in-page SVG.\nSource is stashed in dataset.src before mermaid.run() replaces it with SVG.\n\nKeeps the render's svg id intact: mermaid's <style> is id-scoped, so\nstripping the id was dropping every themed fill back to default black.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","what_changed":"","facets":{"component":[],"flow":[],"theme":[]},"refs":{"files":["site/index.html"],"pitfall":null,"related":[]},"source":"hook","enriched":false,"confidence":"EXTRACTED"}
